ck into compliance.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026324771","violation_type_title":"Safety - Electrical Outlets Covered (26 TAC §746.3701(1))","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-134860-i20220303-v2","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-3401-a","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-134860-i20220303","date":"2022-03-03","original_code":"746.3401(a)","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2022-03-03","finding":"Annual Sanitation Inspection: The last sanitation inspection availabe for review was from 8/18/20.  The operation did not have a current sanitation inspection.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026444882","violation_type_title":"Annual Sanitation Inspection (26 TAC §746.3401(a))","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-134860-i20220303-v3","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-5531","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-134860-i20220303","date":"2022-03-03","original_code":"746.5531","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Corrected at inspection","finding":"Child-Care Center Must be Equipped with a Working Carbon Monoxide (CO) Detection System: During the inspection the carbon monoxide detector wasn't working.  This was corrected during the inspection by putting new batteries into the carbon monoxide detector, placing the operation back into compliance.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026525223","violation_type_title":"Child-Care Center Must be Equipped with a Working Carbon Monoxide (CO) Detection System (26 TAC §746.5531)","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"}]}],"geo":{"state":{"code":"TX","name":"Texas"},"county":{"fips":"48275","name":"Knox County"},"zip":"76371","city":"Munday"},"related":{"same_operator":[],"same_operator_total":0,"same_building":[],"same_address_other_authority":[],"nearby":[]}}
